// Machine-specific exclusions. Deliberately empty -- every line here belongs
// to THIS machine alone.
//
// Unlike .stignore, this file survives an update: install_service.sh creates
// it when it is missing and never touches an existing one, whereas the
// packaged .stignore is authoritative and gets offered for overwriting.
//
// .stignore pulls this file in with "#include", placed high up there on
// purpose: the FIRST matching pattern decides a file's fate, so patterns
// written here take precedence over the general ones and can also make an
// exception from them. Only the line for the credentials sits above the
// include and is therefore out of reach from here.
//
// The file excludes itself from the synchronisation, so what one machine
// selects never reaches the others.
//
// Main use: keeping single project paths under projects/ off this machine.
// How to write an entry -- and the order to follow when the thing to exclude
// has already been synchronised -- is described in the README.
